  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Runner initialization, query preprocessing, multipart images, and safe header diagnostics\n- Initialize runners with ILoggerFactory or ILogger<JevRunner>, or read API keys from an environment variable (JEV_TOKEN by default).\n- Generate query APIs for IJevQueryProcessRequestBeforeExecution implementations without requiring JevQueryAttribute. Process the completed request immediately before execution and use the returned request.\n- Log outgoing request, client-default, and content headers at debug level, redacting credential headers and API-key occurrences before logging.\n- Breaking: Request.Execute(apiKey, ...) now accepts ILoggerFactory instead of ILogger<JevRunner>; use a factory or execute through an explicitly initialized runner.\n- Add regression coverage for initialization, query preprocessing, and credential-safe header diagnostics.\n- Upload file-backed and byte-backed images as multipart data alongside inline Base64 assets.\n- Prepare images independently with CreateAssetWithAdjustments, read assets with ReadAsBytes, and automatically register AssetAndStateReference query properties in AssetState. JEV007 warns about incompatible state types.\n- Breaking: AddImageAsset requires base64Encode; AddImageAssetWithAutoAdjustment is synchronous; Asset.Name is now Asset.AssetName.\n- Fix double-serialized request bodies and preserve literal backtick references in outgoing JSON and debug logs.",
